      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A national wealth tax is a powerful tool to directly reduce inequality by targeting the accumulated assets of the ultra-wealthy rather than just their income. While critics argue it might stifle investment, the evidence shows that a well-designed tax with low rates and exemptions for productive capital actually encourages long-term economic growth while redistributing power. Ultimately, this policy is the most effective way to ensure that the benefits of economic success are shared across the entire nation, not hoarded by a tiny elite.",
